From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iot_ab: write the boot-control record only when it changes

On block devices the success mark rewrote the record at every kernel
hand-off, even when the slot was already marked good. A power loss
during that write can tear the record, which BL2 then resets to slot
A, possibly an older firmware image package. Skip the write when the
slot's tries is already zero, as the MTD path does.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
--- a/boot/iot_ab.c
+++ b/boot/iot_ab.c
@@ -92,7 +92,8 @@
 							? PART_BOOT_B : PART_BOOT_A;
 		bctrl->tries[bctrl->slot_suffix] = BOOTCTRL_SRC;
 		iot_ab_handle_blctrl(dev_desc, part_info, bctrl);
-	} else if (type == BOOTCTRL_FINISH) {
+	} else if (type == BOOTCTRL_FINISH &&
+		   bctrl->tries[bctrl->slot_suffix] != BOOTCTRL_BOOT_SUCCESS) {
 		bctrl->tries[bctrl->slot_suffix] = BOOTCTRL_BOOT_SUCCESS;
 		iot_ab_handle_blctrl(dev_desc, part_info, bctrl);
 	}
